OL,3,GNEWSAThe hero dinner lady who died
OL,4,Asaving five children in the Aberfan
OL,5,Adisaster
OL,6,
OL,7,FOn 21 October 1966, as a primary school
OL,8,Fand surrounding homes in Aberfan were
OL,9,Fengulfed by slurry from a collapsed
OL,10,Fcoal tip, a dinner lady was collecting
OL,11,Fmoney from pupils.
OL,13,FWithin moments, 144 people were dead,
OL,14,Fincluding 116 children, on what was the
OL,15,Flast day of class at Pantglas Junior
OL,16,FSchool before the half-term holiday.
OL,18,FBut five children were saved that day
OL,19,Fby the heroic actions of Nansi
OL,20,FWilliams, who died shielding the group.
OL,23,APub: 15-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
